Title: The Lighthouse Keeper's Daughter
Credit: Book and lyrics by
Author: An OpenAct sample script
Draft date: Workshop draft

> ACT ONE <

.SCENE 1: THE HARBOUR WALL

Gulls, nets and a supply boat that comes once a week. The ISLANDERS mend, haul and gossip.

!SONG 1: SALT AND STONE (COMPANY)
[[openact: song | singers: COMPANY | function: Opening number: the island, and the people it keeps | staging: Full company on the harbour wall | feel: Work song; stamped rhythm]]

.SCENE 2: THE LAMP ROOM, SKERRY LIGHTHOUSE

Night. The great lens turns slowly overhead. TOMAS trims the wick with a care that has lasted thirty years. MAREN sits on the stair with a letter she keeps folding and unfolding.

TOMAS
You've read that letter so many times the ink's going grey.

MAREN
They want me in September. A place at the conservatoire. Fees paid.

TOMAS
And who keeps the light while you're playing your fiddle in a city?

MAREN
You've kept it alone before.

TOMAS
(Quietly)
That was the worst year of my life.

He goes out onto the gallery. The beam sweeps past him, out over the dark water. MAREN unfolds the letter one more time.

!SONG 2: FURTHER THAN THE LIGHT (MAREN)
[[openact: song | singers: MAREN | function: "I want" song: Maren's wish to leave the island, and her guilt about it | staging: Maren climbs to the gallery rail; the beam sweeps the audience on each chorus | feel: Folk ballad; solo fiddle building to full band]]

~Every night I count the ships
~That pass and never stay,
~Every night I hold the light
~For someone sailing away.
~Just once I want to be the one
~Who goes into the night,
~And finds out what the dark is hiding
~Further than the light.

The beam passes. When it comes round again, TOMAS is standing in the doorway. He has heard every word.

TOMAS
Your mother sang that tune. Not those words. But that tune.

.SCENE 3: THE JETTY, NEXT MORNING

Grey dawn. AGNES ties up the supply boat: crates of tins and a sack of post.

AGNES
Post for the lighthouse! And something that looks very much like a ticket.

!SONG 2a: FURTHER THAN THE LIGHT (REPRISE) (MAREN, TOMAS)
[[openact: song | singers: MAREN, TOMAS | function: Placeholder: father and daughter, lyrics to come | staging:  | feel: Stripped back; fiddle and voice | reprise: yes]]

